    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T14:22:17Z",
    "body": "Merged main at 17f6ce33. The conflict was real: main's #1174 added `post::dialect::WorkVoice` / `work_voice()` and said \"#1199 settles undeclared scripts for good\". This PR had added its own `declared_turning()`.\n\n**Resolution.** Took main's `dialect.rs` as it stands and dropped `declared_turning`. `lathe_voice::at_post` now matches on `WorkVoice`:\n- `ToolSpindle` passes.\n- `WorkSpindle` is held to the door.\n- `Undeclared` is held on a lathe or mill-turn, with the refusal naming the missing `capabilities` line. It passes elsewhere.\n\n**Behaviour change from the earlier head:** masks 0 and 4 are now Undeclared, as main reads them, so they are held on a work-spindle machine rather than passed as a mill post. That's the stricter reading. The pin covers 0 and 4 explicitly, and the decision file is updated.\n\n**Main's matrix test** `lathe_workholding_mill_post::every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict`: for an undeclared script, a milling (tool) section on a chucked machine is now refused by the lathe door first, by name, exactly as for a declared turning post, so it no longer reaches the chuck-rpm judgement. Its expected verdict is updated (`!chucked`). The program is still refused.\n\n**Gate on the merged head** (debug, this Mac):\n- Unit tests: lathe_voice 4 and post dialect 3.\n- App suites: posting 17, lathe_post_refusals 11, lathe_work_spindle 5, lathe_workholding_mill_post 3, lathe_workholding_live 3, lathe_workholding_kinds 10 (1 ignored), per_op_files 9, setup_mounts_post 6, conformance 6.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --lib --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\nAuthor-side note, not a review. Ready again for NeoTech's review. (M5)\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
